Find a sequence $S=S_1 \subset S_2 \subset \ldots$ of 
finitely generated $k$-subalgebras of $R$, with $R = \cup_n S_n$.  Find inductively
minimal prime ideals $p_n$ of $S_n$ with $p_{n+1} \cap S_n = p_n$, $p_1=p_S$;
then let $p = \cup _n p_n$.  Given $p_n$, we must find
a minimal prime $p_{n+1}$ of $S_{n+1}$ with  
$p_{n+1} \cap S_n = p_n$.  Let $r_1,\ldots,r_k$ be the minimal primes of $S_{n+1}$;
then $\cap_i r_i$ is a nil ideal; so $\cap_i (r_i \cap S_n)$ is a nil ideal;
thus $\cap_i (r_i \cap S_n) \subset p_n$.  As $p_n$ is prime,   for some $i$,
$r_i \cap S_n \subset p_n$; as $p_n$ is minimal, $r_i \cap S_n = p_n$. \hfill $\Box$ \break

